  "verdict_rationale": "Model-C score progression from P90 to P99 substantially increases the 180-second regime flip probability (from 29.2% at P90 to 27.0% at P99), demonstrating valid macro deterioration discrimination. However, score severity fails to localize the reversal-entry zone: median remaining prevailing excursion remains heavy (+2.04 ATR at P99 vs +1.78 ATR at P90), median delay to a broad winning zone remains protracted (15s at P99 vs 110s at P90), immediate fade expectancy remains deeply negative (-0.032 ATR at P99 vs -0.016 ATR at P90), and over 57% of regimes continue extending >=1.00 ATR even after crossing P99. Therefore, P90 was NOT simply 'too early' on a monotonic timing curve; Model C inherently reflects macro deterioration velocity rather than local turning-point geometry, and moving deeper into the score tail does not make the signal economically actionable without an independent causal timing mechanism.",
